{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Software Engineering Main Concepts"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear every time you discuss about main concepts of software engineering."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understands systems theories, business processes and basic concepts on IT.  Create a map of processes that allows identifying areas in an information system, using IT tools to generate reports based on the company's needs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands simple information in slow conversations about the communicative topics and vocabulary related to this level. Exchanges simple information on IT concepts, systems theory, and diagrams of processes."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about main software engineering concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Describe what each concept is about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write what the importance of those concepts for software engineering is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your poster with the class and discuss about other main concepts."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about main software engineering concepts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I describe what each concept is about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand what the importance of those concepts is."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Demonstratives as Pronouns and Adjectives</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">demonstratives</span> as pronouns to express the distance between the speaker and the noun. Demonstrative pronouns are those that identify or point at things and persons. In addition, you can use demonstratives as adjectives to give a characteristic to a noun."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The demonstrative pronouns and demonstrative adjectives use the same words, but they differ in the position within a sentence and the intended meaning. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"NEAR \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"FAR\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">SINGULAR</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">This</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">PLURAL </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">These</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Those</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are singular and plural demonstratives that you can use according to the distance: if it is near or far from your position. Look at the following examples: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">You need to store the information of <span class=\"strong\">this </span> document in the cloud. (the document is near the speaker.)<br>  <span class=\"strong\">That </span> provides information to different users. (The program or application is far from the speaker.) </div></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Use demonstrative pronouns </span> to identify and replace nouns.  In order to replace nouns, you have to make sure to leave the context clear so that there are no ambiguities. Look at the following examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\">The records</span> are easy to find with the database. = <span class=\"strong\">These </span>are easy to find with the use of query language. <br>  <span class=\"strong\">Clouds provide application software; this </span>is an advantage.  <br>  Web systems works with <span class=\"strong\">a cache. This</span> is an in-memory store that contains information. </div></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the contrary, the <span class=\"strong\">demonstrative adjectives </span> modify the noun and help us indicate the position of something related to ours. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">This technique </span> is effective to store information.<br> <span class=\"strong\">That internal memory </span>stores a subset of information. <br> <span class=\"strong\">These concurrency is </span> part of application processes. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Those devices </span> are associated to the Cloud Computing. </div></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " So, the difference between these demonstratives is that the demonstrative adjectives are always placed before a noun while the demonstrative pronouns are placed before a verb."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That SSL code means secure socket layer."}, {"type": "example", "content": " This program uses a platform as a service, and it allows cloud computing."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Software Engineering: Main Concepts</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Software engineering involves different and multiple processes for software production. There are common concepts to test, implement and develop a software, let's have a look at them."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Concept </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">What is it?</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Common uses and examples</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Relational Databases\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A collection of data items. These ones are organized in tables that contain information. You can access information or put it back together without the necessity of organizing the tables. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li>Order management systems </li> <li>Corporate Data bases: business, to register profits and losses. </li> </ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Security\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It contains the verification of the user's identity or authentication, the permissions or authorizations, and the information transmission. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li>Website browsers: banks transactions, Firefox browser </li> <li>OAuth protocol to enable workers of a company to access information. </li> </ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Cloud Computing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is a type of Internet-based computing service that gives a group of computers and similar devices the resources to process information. It processes data from different companies.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul> <li>Infrastructure as a service (IaaS): Xen, Oracle VirtualBox, Oracle VM. </li>  <li>Platform as a service (PaaS): Microsoft Azure and Google App Engine. </li>  <li>Software as a service (SaaS): customers get access to application software and databases through a common cloud. </li> </ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Concurrency\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It has to do with parallelism inside the application. It is a group of techniques that permit a program to run different tasks simultaneously.  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Java implements concurrency using different threads, which are placeholders of information associated with a single use of a program that can manage multiple concurrent users. For example, the concurrency library of core Java.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Caching\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is an internal memory that saves subcategories of information. These are commonly stored in a database. It helps to generate results based on information from the database at a cheaper price. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To distribute information, modern web applications, such as Facebook, work with the caching system called Memcached.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hashing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It helps to the fast access to data. It facilitates the search of data organized in a sequence of large files.  It is also used to place data in a cloud system.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hash functions are used in Google's indexing service; each URL is hashed to  a particular computer.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "encrypted "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something encoded, normally sent as a message"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Internet security supports authentication, authorization, and information transmission that is often encrypted via SSL."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "store "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to save or put in storage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cache is a part of the local internal memory that helps us to store information from database subcategories."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "simultaneously "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at the same time as"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Concurrency is the ability of a database to allow multiple users to make multiple transactions simultaneously. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "socket "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "part of a two-way communication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I remember that SSL code means Secure Socket Layer.  SSL is a process that we use to recognize passwords in a website."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cache "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "locally stored information, used to help speed things up"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The cache is a part of the local internal memory that helps us to store information from database subcategories."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n1le01ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": 