a": [{"type": "text", "content": "you"}], "id": 4}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "fast"}], "id": 5}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "access"}], "id": 6}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "to"}], "id": 7}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "data."}], "id": 8}], "id": 2}], "type": "WSB", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Describing Important Aspects of the Main Software Concepts "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Activity 2"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">\nOrganize the mystery sentence.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Move each word to place it in the correct order.</span> \n<br>\nYou have 2 attempts to submit your answers."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12}], "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n1le01ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher </span>: Let's discuss some software engineering concepts. So, it\u2018s time for you to ask questions.\n<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Student </span>: I have a list of the main concepts. These include relational databases, security, cloud computing, concurrency, caching, and hashing. Those aren't clear enough to me. Could you give me a brief definition of them, please?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Teacher </span>: Yes, those are just six. Let's start with relational databases. These are collections of data items that are organized as a group of tables from which you can access data. The security protocol is also important because a person or company can exchange and protect confidential information. In general, internet security supports authentication, authorization, and information transmission that is often encrypted via SSL. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Student </span>: I remember that SSL code means Secure Socket Layer.  SSL is a process that we use to recognize passwords in a website."}, {"time": "66000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher </span>: Yes, that's true. Cloud computing is another useful and popular concept these days. With this, you can store and access data and programs over the Internet without the necessity of using your computer's hard drive. <br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Student </span>: I think Microsoft Azure is a good example of if. This program uses a platform as a service, and it allows cloud computing.  <br><span class=\"strong\">Teacher </span>: Correct. We also have concurrency. Concurrency is the ability of a database to allow multiple users to make multiple transactions simultaneously. This is one of the main properties that differentiates a database, such as the Java library, from other types of data storage, such as spreadsheets. Now, can you tell what caching and hashing are? <br>"}, {"time": "116000", "image": "enpe8n1le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Student </span>: Caching comes from 'cache'. The cache is a part of the local internal memory that helps us to store information from database subcategories. Hashing, for its part, is a programming function that we use to find and place information into large files. <br><span class=\"strong\">Teacher </span>: Good. So, after studying these concepts, why do you think software engineering is so important? <br><span class=\"strong\">Student </span>: Well, it's important because it aims to satisfy the needs of the users successfully. It offers them the possibility to control their networks in the most efficient, effective, and easiest way. To sum up, it reduces complexity, it is safe, and it helps companies to increase their productivity! <br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n1le01ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}